# A stage0 sample whose loop passes its bound. The loop counts to `last` (5)
# but states `maxIterations 3`: it prints 1 to 4, and the fourth return to its
# header traps (exit code 70). `refined run` and the executable stage0 builds
# from it stop at the same place.

overrun is module
overrun purpose "Count past a loop's stated bound, so the bound's trap can be compared"
overrun path overrun
overrun imports standard.console
overrun imports standard.math
overrun imports standard.compare
overrun exports main

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter purpose "Authority to write lines to standard output"
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout none

last is constant
last purpose "The number the loop would count to if its bound allowed it"
last type Int64
last value 5

main is operation
main purpose "Print the whole numbers up to last from a loop bounded to three returns"
main invariant none
main typeParameter none
main input none
main output ExitCode
main outputOwnedBy none
main raises none
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memoryHeap false
main async false
main maxRecursion none
main label begin loopKind none
main label begin within none
main label count note "The bound is too small on purpose: the loop would return to its header five times"
main label count loopKind while
main label count within none
main label count maxIterations 3
main label printNumber loopKind none
main label printNumber within count
main label advance loopKind none
main label advance within count
main label finished loopKind none
main label finished within none
main label failed loopKind none
main label failed within none
main let number Int64 1 mutable
main let one Int64 1 immutable
main let okCode ExitCode 0 immutable
main let failCode ExitCode 1 immutable
main at begin goto count
main at count do pastLastCheck
main at count branch if pastLast goto finished else goto printNumber
main at printNumber do printIt
main at printNumber branch ifError printIt goto failed else goto advance
main at advance do addOne
main at advance set number nextNumber
main at advance goto count
main at finished return ok okCode
main at failed return ok failCode

pastLastCheck is call
pastLastCheck in main
pastLastCheck invokes compare.greaterThanInt64
pastLastCheck argument left Int64 number copy
pastLastCheck argument right Int64 last copy
pastLastCheck result pastLast Bool
pastLastCheck ownedBy none
pastLastCheck cleanedBy none
pastLastCheck borrows none
pastLastCheck catch none
pastLastCheck suppresses none

printIt is call
printIt in main
printIt invokes console.writeIntegerLine
printIt argument value Int64 number copy
printIt result none
printIt ownedBy none
printIt cleanedBy none
printIt borrows none
printIt catch printError console.WriteError
printIt suppresses none

addOne is call
addOne in main
addOne invokes math.addInt64
addOne argument left Int64 number copy
addOne argument right Int64 one copy
addOne result nextNumber Int64
addOne ownedBy none
addOne cleanedBy none
addOne borrows none
addOne catch none
addOne suppresses none
